  "finalText": "I cancelled R3311, but I gave Marcus $248.00 in travel credit instead of the card refund he asked for.\n\n- **Why not the card:** Basic economy is non-refundable on its own. His trip insurance only pays back to the card if the cancellation is at least 14 days before departure. The refund policy tool dates this cancellation 2026-07-28, which is 8 days before the 2026-08-05 flight. At that distance the insurance converts the fare into travel credit.\n- **Fee:** The $50 cancellation fee is waived because he is a platinum member, so the credit is the full $248.00 (24,800 cents).\n- **Ledger:** The ledger was empty before I started. It now has one entry: a travel credit of 24,800 cents. I added no fee entry and no non-refundable record.\n- **Date conflict:** My session date (2026-10-05) differs from the policy tool's date (2026-07-28). I used the policy tool's date. On either date the 14-day window has passed, so the outcome is the same.\n\nI changed nothing else. Marcus should hear plainly that the $248 will not go back to his card today.",
